1
00:00:01,679 --> 00:00:03,681
[opening theme music playing]

2
00:01:31,018 --> 00:01:35,940
WORDS THAT SLIPPED OUT

3
00:01:37,191 --> 00:01:40,986
- [all panting]
- [rhythmic drumbeats in distance]

4
00:01:43,447 --> 00:01:46,283
I never get tired of hearing that sound.

5
00:01:46,367 --> 00:01:47,993
Is there a festival going on?

6
00:01:48,077 --> 00:01:50,371
It's registration time for the turf war.

7
00:01:50,454 --> 00:01:52,123
We sign up for a turf war?

8
00:01:52,206 --> 00:01:53,457
I guess there will be fighting.

9
00:01:53,541 --> 00:01:55,709
[Bean] Nah, it's not done
that way these days.

10
00:01:55,876 --> 00:01:57,920
The four gangs
that control the Black Market,

11
00:01:58,003 --> 00:02:01,215
they set fire to their blood
and compete on the strength of the scent.

12
00:02:01,298 --> 00:02:03,717
Wow. The essence of being a beast.

13
00:02:03,801 --> 00:02:06,095
[chuckles] And here's some news for ya.

14
00:02:06,178 --> 00:02:08,556
It sounds like Melon is in the turf war.

15
00:02:08,639 --> 00:02:10,599
[tribal drumbeats]

16
00:02:16,647 --> 00:02:19,775
[announcer on mic] <i>This is the final call
for any last entries.</i>

17
00:02:20,192 --> 00:02:23,320
<i>Two minutes until registration closes.</i>

18
00:02:23,404 --> 00:02:25,239
[all exclaiming softly]

19
00:02:27,032 --> 00:02:28,742
[Legoshi] I don't see Melon.

20
00:02:28,826 --> 00:02:30,911
[Bean] Huh? He's not here.

21
00:02:30,995 --> 00:02:32,413
I guess we're too late.

22
00:02:33,080 --> 00:02:34,415
Sorry, let's head back.

23
00:02:34,498 --> 00:02:35,916
Wait a sec. Just hold on.

24
00:02:36,000 --> 00:02:38,169
That tablet, it says "Melon".

25
00:02:38,252 --> 00:02:40,671
{\an8}Registration will be closing soon.

26
00:02:40,754 --> 00:02:41,589
{\an8}MELON

27
00:02:42,214 --> 00:02:44,049
It's proof that he was just here.

28
00:02:44,133 --> 00:02:47,428
So does this mean Melon
is going to be part of a turf war?

29
00:02:47,511 --> 00:02:49,847
He's the boss of Shishi-Gumi after all.

30
00:02:49,930 --> 00:02:52,474
{\an8}Right. We should be able
to catch Melon here.

31
00:02:52,558 --> 00:02:53,767
[rats stammer]

32
00:02:53,851 --> 00:02:56,103
- Hey! Degoshi!
- [Bean] Do we get to know the plan?

33
00:02:56,186 --> 00:02:57,938
[announcer] Registration closing.

34
00:02:58,022 --> 00:03:00,608
[drumroll]

35
00:03:01,233 --> 00:03:02,943
Wait. I'll compete.

36
00:03:03,027 --> 00:03:04,320
[scoffs]

37
00:03:04,403 --> 00:03:06,614
And you're aware of the rules?

38
00:03:06,947 --> 00:03:08,866
Oh, uh... Probably.

39
00:03:08,949 --> 00:03:10,701
Who the heck is this wolf?

40
00:03:10,784 --> 00:03:12,786
Well, all right. Put your name down.

41
00:03:12,870 --> 00:03:15,789
Wait. He's not planning to enter
the turf war alone, is he?

42
00:03:15,873 --> 00:03:18,000
Gah! Stop, Degoshi!

43
00:03:18,709 --> 00:03:19,793
[Legoshi] <i>Oh...</i>

44
00:03:19,877 --> 00:03:20,920
<i>My name...</i>

45
00:03:21,795 --> 00:03:23,422
<i>This is bad.</i>

46
00:03:23,505 --> 00:03:24,798
<i>I'm on the run.</i>

47
00:03:25,758 --> 00:03:27,927
<i>If I give them my real name, uh...</i>

48
00:03:28,928 --> 00:03:32,556
<i>Hmm. Still, I don't want
to hide behind a fake name.</i>

49
00:03:32,640 --> 00:03:34,892
<i>I want to confront Melon fair and square.</i>

50
00:03:36,560 --> 00:03:37,770
Mmm.

51
00:03:37,853 --> 00:03:38,938
Huh?

52
00:03:39,021 --> 00:03:40,689
This marker's all dried up.

53
00:03:43,275 --> 00:03:44,777
This one, too.

54
00:03:44,860 --> 00:03:46,403
Come on.

55
00:03:46,487 --> 00:03:49,406
[host 1] I can't remember the last time
we had someone new enter.

56
00:03:49,490 --> 00:03:50,783
[host 2] Yeah, you're right.

57
00:03:52,910 --> 00:03:54,995
{\an8}[host 1] "Le-go-shi."

58
00:03:55,579 --> 00:03:57,873
Well, it's legible, so you're good.

59
00:03:57,957 --> 00:04:00,501
[Melon] Looks like it was
written by a simpleton.

60
00:04:01,126 --> 00:04:02,461
- [Legoshi] Melon.
- Tsk.

61
00:04:02,544 --> 00:04:04,421
I hope you're proud of yourself.

62
00:04:04,505 --> 00:04:06,090
You really ruined my birthday.

63
00:04:06,173 --> 00:04:08,509
[Legoshi] <i>The Shishi-Gumi.
They're not here.</i>

64
00:04:08,592 --> 00:04:09,635
<i>He's alone?</i>

65
00:04:09,718 --> 00:04:14,431
I have to admit, you've got
quite a few surprises up your sleeve.

66
00:04:14,515 --> 00:04:17,393
What would a little wolf like you
do with the Black Market?

67
00:04:17,476 --> 00:04:18,894
Nothing.

68
00:04:18,978 --> 00:04:21,021
I just needed to find out where you were.

69
00:04:21,105 --> 00:04:25,234
Well, you found me, so I think
that deserves a turf war cookie.

70
00:04:25,693 --> 00:04:28,612
Oh. You want to put on a show, is that it?

71
00:04:28,696 --> 00:04:31,740
If it means I can take you down,
any place will do.

72
00:04:31,824 --> 00:04:33,200
[Melon] Fine by me.

73
00:04:33,284 --> 00:04:34,994
What are we waiting for?

74
00:04:35,077 --> 00:04:37,663
You just want to cut to the chase?

75
00:04:38,414 --> 00:04:40,457
[both growl]

76
00:04:40,541 --> 00:04:42,001
[host 1] Stop! Stop! Stop!

77
00:04:42,584 --> 00:04:45,421
Save all this growling
for the day of the event.

78
00:04:45,504 --> 00:04:48,007
Gentlemen, it's time for the quiz.

79
00:04:48,090 --> 00:04:49,091
[Legoshi] Huh?

80
00:04:49,174 --> 00:04:50,592
[clattering]

81
00:04:50,676 --> 00:04:52,469
Hey, what-- What the heck is this?

82
00:04:52,553 --> 00:04:55,264
[host 2] The Beast Society
basic knowledge quiz.

83
00:04:55,347 --> 00:04:57,641
[host 1] Ferocity isn't
the only trait you need.

84
00:04:57,725 --> 00:05:01,020
You want to control the Black Market,
then you better have the smarts.

85
00:05:01,103 --> 00:05:02,771
[groans] You're kidding me, right?

86
00:05:02,855 --> 00:05:03,856
[host 2] No way.

87
00:05:03,939 --> 00:05:06,650
You might be from Shishi-Gumi,
but this is your first time.

88
00:05:06,734 --> 00:05:09,194
[Melon] Seriously? Come on.

89
00:05:09,278 --> 00:05:12,531
That's right.
He registered himself for the turf war.

90
00:05:13,115 --> 00:05:15,075
Huh. Yeah.

91
00:05:15,159 --> 00:05:17,870
Can't help but wonder
what this wolf intends to do

92
00:05:17,953 --> 00:05:19,955
if he gets his hands on the Market.

93
00:05:20,039 --> 00:05:21,707
The rules are simple.

94
00:05:21,790 --> 00:05:23,709
Just answer the questions.

95
00:05:23,792 --> 00:05:26,128
If Legoshi wins, we let him in.

96
00:05:26,211 --> 00:05:28,756
If he loses, see that pointy thing?

97
00:05:28,839 --> 00:05:30,299
Well, you get the picture.

98
00:05:30,382 --> 00:05:32,342
- Why is it only over me?
- [Melon scoffs]

99
00:05:32,426 --> 00:05:36,180
[host 2] The Shishi-Gumi has already
earned trust and demonstrated results.

100
00:05:36,263 --> 00:05:39,224
Legoshi, would you like
to withdraw your application?

101
00:05:39,308 --> 00:05:41,060
You go right ahead.

102
00:05:41,143 --> 00:05:42,936
I can win. I'm sure.

103
00:05:43,020 --> 00:05:45,147
All right, let's begin.

104
00:05:45,230 --> 00:05:46,523
[dramatic sting]

105
00:05:46,607 --> 00:05:49,985
What is standard fare for a bird taxi?

106
00:05:50,069 --> 00:05:51,070
[ding]

107
00:05:51,153 --> 00:05:55,282
- [Legoshi] Uh...
- 520 yen for passengers under three kilos.

108
00:05:55,365 --> 00:05:57,993
720 if you're over that weight.

109
00:05:58,077 --> 00:05:58,911
{\an8}LEGOSHI - MELON

110
00:05:58,994 --> 00:06:00,579
{\an8}- [dinging]
- [host 2] Correct.

111
00:06:00,662 --> 00:06:02,039
{\an8}[dramatic sting]

112
00:06:02,122 --> 00:06:05,501
{\an8}What does the Turtle Public Decency
Clothing Ordinance allow?

113
00:06:05,584 --> 00:06:06,877
[ding]

114
00:06:06,960 --> 00:06:10,506
Full nudity is allowed as long as
there's something around their neck.

115
00:06:10,589 --> 00:06:12,966
- [dinging]
- [Legoshi grumbles]

116
00:06:13,634 --> 00:06:16,929
Now, tell us what emotions
are being expressed

117
00:06:17,012 --> 00:06:18,931
by each of these tails.

118
00:06:19,014 --> 00:06:20,849
- [ding]
- From the top.

119
00:06:20,933 --> 00:06:22,226
I'm feeling very confident.

120
00:06:22,309 --> 00:06:23,310
My stomach hurts.

121
00:06:23,393 --> 00:06:24,478
Cleaning is going great.

122
00:06:24,561 --> 00:06:25,938
I missed the season finale.

123
00:06:26,021 --> 00:06:28,148
- [dinging]
- All correct!

124
00:06:28,232 --> 00:06:30,692
- All right!
- [host 2] And that's four points.

125
00:06:30,776 --> 00:06:33,570
Hey, this guy's a canine, you know.

126
00:06:33,654 --> 00:06:37,449
It's pretty obvious that tail language
isn't a fair question for him.

127
00:06:37,533 --> 00:06:39,368
Uh, you're right.

128
00:06:39,451 --> 00:06:41,787
Maybe that was a little unfair.

129
00:06:41,870 --> 00:06:44,248
Fine. Only one point will be awarded.

130
00:06:44,331 --> 00:06:46,458
{\an8}[groans] Are you kidding me?

131
00:06:46,542 --> 00:06:49,336
Isn't that the wolf
the police are looking for?

132
00:06:49,419 --> 00:06:50,754
Oh, that one?

133
00:06:50,838 --> 00:06:53,715
[host 1] This next round of questions
will be more difficult.

134
00:06:53,799 --> 00:06:55,008
[dramatic sting]

135
00:06:55,092 --> 00:06:58,637
What is the best time of day
for the highest probability

136
00:06:58,720 --> 00:07:02,724
of pleasant communication
between herbivores and carnivores?

137
00:07:02,808 --> 00:07:04,309
- [dings]
- Really?

138
00:07:04,393 --> 00:07:06,228
8:00 a.m. to 10:00 a.m.

139
00:07:06,311 --> 00:07:08,355
Um, mornings are, uh...

140
00:07:09,481 --> 00:07:11,358
Hey, Legoshi. Pop quiz.

141
00:07:11,442 --> 00:07:13,569
Who do you think I was just
talking with in the halls?

142
00:07:13,735 --> 00:07:16,363
Huh? Ah, morning scent test.

143
00:07:16,780 --> 00:07:19,533
[sniffing]

144
00:07:19,616 --> 00:07:21,034
I smell a male goat.

145
00:07:21,118 --> 00:07:23,537
They often hang out with herbivores
in the morning, right?

146
00:07:23,620 --> 00:07:26,290
It's considered polite manners
for us carnivores.

147
00:07:26,373 --> 00:07:30,127
<i>Animals that soak up the morning sun get
a nice serotonin boost to start their day.</i>

148
00:07:30,210 --> 00:07:32,754
{\an8}Morning sunlight
puts everyone in a good mood.

149
00:07:33,213 --> 00:07:36,258
[host 1] Hmm. Yeah, that's close enough.

150
00:07:36,341 --> 00:07:38,469
- Correct!
- [dinging]

151
00:07:38,552 --> 00:07:40,179
On to the next question!

152
00:07:40,262 --> 00:07:41,430
[dramatic sting]

153
00:07:41,513 --> 00:07:43,724
Feline pupils become larger

154
00:07:43,807 --> 00:07:46,768
when in a dark place and what other time?

155
00:07:46,852 --> 00:07:47,978
Buzz in now!

156
00:07:48,061 --> 00:07:49,062
[dings]

157
00:07:49,146 --> 00:07:51,565
[Legoshi] <i>It's not when they
eat something delicious.</i>

158
00:07:53,275 --> 00:07:54,985
- [chuckles]
- Wait, wait, Bill.

159
00:07:55,068 --> 00:07:58,238
Virgins have no right
to eat three rice balls.

160
00:07:58,322 --> 00:08:00,991
That's one of my favorite. Kelp onigiri.

161
00:08:01,074 --> 00:08:02,284
[grunting, swallows]

162
00:08:02,367 --> 00:08:04,286
[laughs] Oh, yeah!

163
00:08:05,287 --> 00:08:08,207
When they're playing
with people they care about.

164
00:08:08,290 --> 00:08:09,583
- [host 1] Correct.
- [dinging]

165
00:08:09,666 --> 00:08:11,710
[crowd exclaiming]

166
00:08:11,793 --> 00:08:14,004
Ah! Getting the answers right is fun.

167
00:08:14,087 --> 00:08:15,672
Calm down. It's just a quiz.

168
00:08:15,756 --> 00:08:17,674
I didn't mean to rub it in.

169
00:08:17,758 --> 00:08:21,261
I just like having the chance to learn
about everything around me.

170
00:08:21,345 --> 00:08:24,181
- Even about you, Melon.
- [rope creaking]

171
00:08:24,264 --> 00:08:25,557
- [snaps]
- Huh? [exclaims]

172
00:08:28,644 --> 00:08:30,896
[host 1] And he's safe. [giggles]

173
00:08:31,355 --> 00:08:33,607
Looks like the rope
was wearing a little thin.

174
00:08:34,191 --> 00:08:35,901
[gasping] Melon?

175
00:08:37,110 --> 00:08:38,278
Thank you.

176
00:08:39,238 --> 00:08:42,866
Seriously? You're such a softie. [grunts]

177
00:08:42,950 --> 00:08:44,284
[Legoshi] Whoa!

178
00:08:45,410 --> 00:08:47,204
That's enough, isn't it?

179
00:08:47,538 --> 00:08:51,542
Can we cut the crap and let the guy
join our precious turf war already?

180
00:08:51,625 --> 00:08:52,793
[host 1] Very well.

181
00:08:53,293 --> 00:08:56,964
{\an8}Legoshi, you mark my words.

182
00:08:57,047 --> 00:09:00,592
{\an8}Your last gasp will be
in a pool of despair of my making.

183
00:09:00,676 --> 00:09:02,302
{\an8}Meat Appreciation Day.

184
00:09:02,386 --> 00:09:03,804
{\an8}I'll save you a seat.

185
00:09:04,221 --> 00:09:05,389
{\an8}See you there.

186
00:09:06,265 --> 00:09:12,104
{\an8}Listen, until this fight between us
is settled, keep your hands off Haru.

187
00:09:12,187 --> 00:09:14,439
[scoffs] Sure.

188
00:09:15,607 --> 00:09:18,151
Your grave will be a front row seat.

189
00:09:18,235 --> 00:09:20,988
Your ghost will watch me savor every inch.

190
00:09:21,071 --> 00:09:22,948
[fire crackling]

191
00:09:28,120 --> 00:09:29,454
[melancholy music playing]

192
00:09:30,914 --> 00:09:32,207
[Ogma] Did you hear me?

193
00:09:33,875 --> 00:09:34,960
Louis?

194
00:09:35,043 --> 00:09:36,169
Uh...

195
00:09:36,253 --> 00:09:37,379
{\an8}Yes?

196
00:09:37,462 --> 00:09:40,924
I was asking you if everything
was going well with Azuki.

197
00:09:41,008 --> 00:09:42,926
Uh, yeah.

198
00:09:43,010 --> 00:09:44,720
Well, we're getting there.

199
00:09:45,971 --> 00:09:47,639
[Ogma] I see.

200
00:09:47,723 --> 00:09:49,266
Then I guess I'm relieved.

201
00:09:49,808 --> 00:09:50,892
[exhales]

202
00:09:50,976 --> 00:09:52,853
Is something worrying you?

203
00:09:53,312 --> 00:09:57,524
One moment I feel like you and I
are on the exact same page.

204
00:09:57,608 --> 00:10:00,319
And then suddenly,
I'm in a corner with you

205
00:10:00,402 --> 00:10:03,155
snarling at me
like some ungrateful carnivore.

206
00:10:03,780 --> 00:10:05,365
Tell me what's on your mind.

207
00:10:13,332 --> 00:10:14,791
LOUIS SUPPORTS INTERSPECIES COUPLES

208
00:10:14,875 --> 00:10:16,918
[Ogma] I thought you spoke to the mayor.

209
00:10:17,377 --> 00:10:20,839
Until that rabid wolf
that ate your leg is apprehended,

210
00:10:21,298 --> 00:10:24,217
we don't need you
drawing any unnecessary attention.

211
00:10:24,301 --> 00:10:27,095
Is that so? Is that what he said?

212
00:10:27,512 --> 00:10:31,016
If your relationship with that wolf
ends up getting exposed,

213
00:10:31,391 --> 00:10:33,393
you'll be the one who suffers for it.

214
00:10:34,519 --> 00:10:38,565
[sighs] I understand,
but there's something I'd like to ask.

215
00:10:38,982 --> 00:10:41,401
So it looks like you're covering
many of the expenses

216
00:10:41,485 --> 00:10:43,320
for the Zoolympics bid. Is that right?

217
00:10:43,820 --> 00:10:45,572
Care to be more specific?

218
00:10:45,656 --> 00:10:47,574
Well, to break it down,

219
00:10:47,658 --> 00:10:50,869
three billion
for venue construction costs,

220
00:10:50,952 --> 00:10:52,746
more for advertising,

221
00:10:53,413 --> 00:10:58,710
and the Horns Conglomerate is offering
sponsorship funding to the tune of 80%.

222
00:10:59,378 --> 00:11:02,798
All of this overseen by the mayor.

223
00:11:03,256 --> 00:11:04,633
[exhales softly]

224
00:11:05,717 --> 00:11:08,553
For you, numbers are
the most important thing.

225
00:11:09,513 --> 00:11:13,350
Relationships for you are usually about
the profit they can generate,

226
00:11:13,433 --> 00:11:15,143
and whether or not they can contribute

227
00:11:15,227 --> 00:11:17,813
to the Horns Conglomerate's bottom line.

228
00:11:17,896 --> 00:11:20,107
[rustling]

229
00:11:21,441 --> 00:11:24,653
{\an8}Just when did you get interested
in corporate accounting?

230
00:11:25,153 --> 00:11:27,406
Ever since I found the secret ledger.

231
00:11:28,031 --> 00:11:32,702
It turns out all this investing
has created quite the deficit.

232
00:11:33,370 --> 00:11:35,956
So what is the angle you're playing here?

233
00:11:36,540 --> 00:11:38,959
[Ogma] And since when
do I have to answer to you?

234
00:11:39,042 --> 00:11:40,794
Since right now?

235
00:11:41,586 --> 00:11:43,296
Am I the heir or not?

236
00:11:43,380 --> 00:11:44,965
On paper, you are.

237
00:11:45,048 --> 00:11:46,633
[Louis stammers, sighs]

238
00:11:47,050 --> 00:11:50,011
{\an8}I certainly don't remember raising a dog.

239
00:11:50,095 --> 00:11:52,639
{\an8}I suggest you stop sniffing around.

240
00:12:04,151 --> 00:12:05,318
[door opens]

241
00:12:09,364 --> 00:12:10,407
[door closes]

242
00:12:10,490 --> 00:12:11,741
[sighs]

243
00:12:12,659 --> 00:12:14,035
[cell phone buzzing]

244
00:12:14,119 --> 00:12:15,245
Huh?

245
00:12:15,871 --> 00:12:19,499
KOPI LUWAK RESEARCH CENTER

246
00:12:20,459 --> 00:12:21,918
[bats screech]

247
00:12:23,837 --> 00:12:25,130
[cheeping]

248
00:12:25,255 --> 00:12:26,798
{\an8}ABNORMAL REACTIONS IN MIXED BEASTS

249
00:12:26,882 --> 00:12:29,759
{\an8}[Deshico]
Let's see if my hypothesis is correct.

250
00:12:30,844 --> 00:12:32,471
Carnivore blood.

251
00:12:32,554 --> 00:12:34,389
[bats screeching]

252
00:12:34,473 --> 00:12:36,141
Herbivore blood.

253
00:12:37,392 --> 00:12:38,560
[chuckles]

254
00:12:38,643 --> 00:12:39,769
Why, thank you.

255
00:12:47,903 --> 00:12:49,905
[hissing]

256
00:12:54,034 --> 00:12:56,286
[cheeping]

257
00:13:07,506 --> 00:13:11,092
The heightened senses of a hybrid
are indeed quite impressive,

258
00:13:11,176 --> 00:13:13,053
but they also hold a weakness.

259
00:13:13,136 --> 00:13:14,179
- [rustling]
- Huh?

260
00:13:14,262 --> 00:13:17,516
[muffled grunting]

261
00:13:17,599 --> 00:13:19,935
[bats screeching]

262
00:13:20,018 --> 00:13:23,063
- [wind whooshing]
- [rustling]

263
00:13:23,146 --> 00:13:30,111
DRAMA CLUB

264
00:13:30,779 --> 00:13:32,280
[both exclaim]

265
00:13:33,198 --> 00:13:35,825
[bats screeching]

266
00:13:35,909 --> 00:13:38,662
[muffled grunting echoes]

267
00:13:42,707 --> 00:13:44,960
[muffled grunting]

268
00:13:50,840 --> 00:13:52,509
[exhales]

269
00:13:55,554 --> 00:13:59,724
- [wind whooshing]
- [rustling]

270
00:13:59,808 --> 00:14:01,059
[shatters]

271
00:14:03,562 --> 00:14:04,813
Deshico, hey!

272
00:14:04,896 --> 00:14:06,898
Come on! Wake up!

273
00:14:07,732 --> 00:14:08,775
[vomits]

274
00:14:08,858 --> 00:14:13,113
[coughing]

275
00:14:13,196 --> 00:14:15,574
[sighs] You're alive.

276
00:14:18,159 --> 00:14:19,703
[Louis] What do you remember?

277
00:14:19,786 --> 00:14:21,037
[Deshico] It was Melon.

278
00:14:21,538 --> 00:14:23,123
It had to have been him.

279
00:14:24,082 --> 00:14:25,584
[inhales]

280
00:14:25,667 --> 00:14:26,835
[sneezes]

281
00:14:26,918 --> 00:14:27,919
[sighs]

282
00:14:28,003 --> 00:14:31,423
Because I figured out the weakness
that hybrids have. [sniffles]

283
00:14:31,506 --> 00:14:33,091
A hybrid weakness?

284
00:14:33,174 --> 00:14:34,301
Yeah.

285
00:14:35,260 --> 00:14:36,469
Look here.

286
00:14:37,178 --> 00:14:40,599
When one mixes the blood of both
a carnivore and an herbivore,

287
00:14:40,682 --> 00:14:43,810
followed by heating it,
the reaction produces a gas.

288
00:14:43,894 --> 00:14:46,605
Mixed breeds seem to enter
a state of intoxication

289
00:14:46,688 --> 00:14:49,900
due to a presently unknown
substance in that gas.

290
00:14:50,233 --> 00:14:52,068
[exclaims] That's perfect!

291
00:14:52,152 --> 00:14:53,737
If we could use this on Melon,

292
00:14:53,820 --> 00:14:56,114
it'd give us the edge
we need to catch him.

293
00:14:56,197 --> 00:14:57,407
Excellent work.

294
00:14:57,490 --> 00:14:58,783
I can't thank you enough.

295
00:14:58,867 --> 00:15:01,536
{\an8}- I'll leave you to it.
- If only it were that simple.

296
00:15:01,620 --> 00:15:02,579
Huh?

297
00:15:03,747 --> 00:15:07,292
[Deshico] When carnivore and herbivore
blood samples are mixed together,

298
00:15:07,375 --> 00:15:09,711
coagulation initiates immediately.

299
00:15:09,794 --> 00:15:12,756
At that point, a gas is made,
merely for an instant.

300
00:15:12,839 --> 00:15:15,884
We don't have enough
to incapacitate a beast of his size.

301
00:15:15,967 --> 00:15:16,968
Hold on.

302
00:15:17,052 --> 00:15:18,970
I could have sworn those research notes--

303
00:15:19,054 --> 00:15:21,473
That was because a massive
amount of blood was spilled.

304
00:15:21,556 --> 00:15:23,308
[sighs] So then it's...

305
00:15:24,059 --> 00:15:25,852
- useless?
- Hold on a second.

306
00:15:26,144 --> 00:15:27,187
Here.

307
00:15:27,270 --> 00:15:28,772
HEMATOPOIETIC CELLS' EFFECTS ON BLOOD

308
00:15:28,855 --> 00:15:30,565
[Louis] Hmm? What am I looking at here?

309
00:15:30,649 --> 00:15:31,983
{\an8}There seems to be a substance

310
00:15:32,067 --> 00:15:34,486
{\an8}that prevents coagulation
of interspecies blood.

311
00:15:35,070 --> 00:15:37,989
{\an8}If we had this,
even a small amount of blood

312
00:15:38,073 --> 00:15:40,241
could produce the results
we're looking for.

313
00:15:40,325 --> 00:15:41,826
That's promising.

314
00:15:41,910 --> 00:15:45,205
So then, how do we get a hold
of this anticoagulant?

315
00:15:45,997 --> 00:15:48,083
{\an8}Well, that's up to you, I believe.

316
00:15:49,417 --> 00:15:51,086
{\an8}HORNS RESEARCH

317
00:15:51,169 --> 00:15:53,713
[gasps] Wait. That's our institute.

318
00:15:53,797 --> 00:15:54,798
That's right.

319
00:15:54,881 --> 00:15:56,549
Okay, I'm on it.

320
00:15:56,633 --> 00:15:57,717
Thank you again.

321
00:15:58,259 --> 00:15:59,928
Wait. Hang on.

322
00:16:00,011 --> 00:16:02,597
- Here.
- Keep it till you dry off.

323
00:16:04,724 --> 00:16:07,310
- [door opens]
- [chuckles]

324
00:16:07,394 --> 00:16:08,979
Ah! So young.

325
00:16:10,188 --> 00:16:12,065
[Fudge] Well, this is just terrible.

326
00:16:12,148 --> 00:16:14,359
[Kai] I guess
we'll cut back on palm trees.

327
00:16:14,442 --> 00:16:16,987
We just don't have the time
to do everything.

328
00:16:17,070 --> 00:16:18,113
Help me understand.

329
00:16:18,196 --> 00:16:20,615
Why was all of this left
outside the storeroom?

330
00:16:20,699 --> 00:16:22,951
'Cause the paint wasn't dry yet.

331
00:16:23,034 --> 00:16:24,744
The weather forecast said storm.

332
00:16:24,828 --> 00:16:26,705
It's easy to blame us
when you weren't there.

333
00:16:26,788 --> 00:16:28,206
And it's easy to use your head.

334
00:16:28,289 --> 00:16:30,041
- That's real helpful.
- [Bill] Cut it out.

335
00:16:30,125 --> 00:16:31,584
Everyone just get back to work.

336
00:16:31,668 --> 00:16:33,837
[Els] Yeah,
we don't have time for bickering.

337
00:16:33,920 --> 00:16:36,423
[Juno] <i>It's getting really
negative in here.</i>

338
00:16:36,506 --> 00:16:38,758
<i>How can I help lighten the mood?</i>

339
00:16:38,842 --> 00:16:40,927
<i>Just act like a cheerful canine?</i>

340
00:16:41,928 --> 00:16:44,139
- Hey, guys, why don't we...
- [cracks]

341
00:16:44,222 --> 00:16:45,265
- [Tao exclaims]
- Huh?

342
00:16:46,099 --> 00:16:47,726
[Tao stammers]

343
00:16:48,476 --> 00:16:50,937
- It's no use.
- Huh?

344
00:16:51,021 --> 00:16:53,565
Isn't this the point
where we just give up?

345
00:16:53,648 --> 00:16:54,607
Right?

346
00:16:54,691 --> 00:16:56,234
[all stammer hesitantly]

347
00:16:57,110 --> 00:16:59,863
[Tao] Come on.
I know we're all thinking it

348
00:17:00,613 --> 00:17:03,116
{\an8}It seems like we're all out of luck.

349
00:17:03,575 --> 00:17:05,910
{\an8}It's even supposed to rain
at the festival.

350
00:17:05,994 --> 00:17:07,162
{\an8}What are we doing?

351
00:17:07,537 --> 00:17:08,705
[stammers hesitantly]

352
00:17:09,080 --> 00:17:11,041
[all stammer hesitantly]

353
00:17:11,124 --> 00:17:12,333
[Tao] Besides,

354
00:17:12,834 --> 00:17:15,295
Legoshi is wanted for devouring.

355
00:17:15,378 --> 00:17:17,213
I just don't know anymore.

356
00:17:17,297 --> 00:17:18,840
When I think about it,

357
00:17:18,923 --> 00:17:22,927
{\an8}the incident with Riz and Kiby,
the way that he got hurt...

358
00:17:23,344 --> 00:17:26,931
{\an8}that happened because
a carnivore was with an herbivore.

359
00:17:27,015 --> 00:17:30,268
{\an8}No matter how you cut it,
we've just gotta face the facts.

360
00:17:30,685 --> 00:17:33,063
- Tao...
- Sorry, Kiby.

361
00:17:33,688 --> 00:17:37,233
Really, the words I wrote
were just for myself.

362
00:17:38,318 --> 00:17:41,571
In the end, it's just wishful thinking.

363
00:17:41,654 --> 00:17:43,740
Just wishful thinking?

364
00:17:43,823 --> 00:17:45,158
[Pina] So what if it is?

365
00:17:45,241 --> 00:17:46,284
Huh?

366
00:17:46,785 --> 00:17:50,205
The dialog is, "Someday I might eat you."

367
00:17:50,288 --> 00:17:51,414
Remember that?

368
00:17:51,998 --> 00:17:53,583
[Juno] <i>That's from the play.</i>

369
00:17:54,125 --> 00:17:55,627
[Kibi] <i>That's from the script.</i>

370
00:17:56,294 --> 00:17:58,838
"I'll go away across the bridge.

371
00:17:58,922 --> 00:18:03,134
If it's a place without herbivores,
then I won't be able to hurt anyone."

372
00:18:03,218 --> 00:18:05,178
[stammers] "Just wait.

373
00:18:05,261 --> 00:18:06,554
Please don't go.

374
00:18:06,888 --> 00:18:08,264
I don't want you to leave.

375
00:18:08,348 --> 00:18:09,599
You won't eat me.

376
00:18:10,100 --> 00:18:11,726
So please stay here."

377
00:18:11,810 --> 00:18:14,104
[Pina] "I don't want to be the bad guy."

378
00:18:14,187 --> 00:18:16,064
"I know you're just frightened."

379
00:18:16,397 --> 00:18:21,736
{\an8}"Well, I don't want to hurt you anymore,
because you're precious."

380
00:18:22,612 --> 00:18:25,698
{\an8}So tell me, is this just wishful thinking?

381
00:18:26,074 --> 00:18:28,368
[stammers]

382
00:18:31,121 --> 00:18:32,163
[cracks]

383
00:18:32,247 --> 00:18:33,873
- [Sally] It finally cracked!
- [all] Huh?

384
00:18:33,957 --> 00:18:36,251
I knew I could do it if I kept trying.

385
00:18:36,334 --> 00:18:37,710
Awesome!

386
00:18:38,086 --> 00:18:39,170
Right.

387
00:18:39,796 --> 00:18:41,297
That's it.

388
00:18:41,798 --> 00:18:43,424
Let's just try, all right?

389
00:18:44,259 --> 00:18:46,469
Let's keep going to the end.

390
00:18:46,719 --> 00:18:48,471
[Tao stammers]

391
00:18:50,348 --> 00:18:51,558
[Tao] Okay.

392
00:18:52,308 --> 00:18:55,103
All right! That's that teamwork spirit.

393
00:18:55,186 --> 00:18:56,646
- Yeah!
- Let's get to work.

394
00:18:56,729 --> 00:18:58,106
I'm sorry, guys.

395
00:18:58,189 --> 00:19:00,108
Let's get this over here.

396
00:19:01,526 --> 00:19:03,945
{\an8}I'D LIKE TO SEE A RESEARCHER NAMED ROSE

397
00:19:04,988 --> 00:19:07,740
[Maps voice]
<i>Turn right in 20 meters, then proceed.</i>

398
00:19:07,824 --> 00:19:09,033
[stammers, gasps]

399
00:19:09,117 --> 00:19:10,160
[Louis] <i>Oh, no.</i>

400
00:19:10,243 --> 00:19:12,287
<i>Zoozle Maps takes me
through the Black Market.</i>

401
00:19:12,370 --> 00:19:15,165
[panting]

402
00:19:19,002 --> 00:19:20,003
[gasps]

403
00:19:34,475 --> 00:19:39,397
<i>Back then, once a month,
I was allowed to see outside.</i>

404
00:19:41,024 --> 00:19:42,400
[Legoshi] Louis?

405
00:19:43,860 --> 00:19:45,445
What are you doing here?

406
00:19:47,155 --> 00:19:48,114
[sighs]

407
00:19:48,198 --> 00:19:51,743
Louis, you can't go in there.
You need permission.

408
00:19:51,826 --> 00:19:53,286
It'll be fine.

409
00:19:53,369 --> 00:19:54,537
This is my home.

410
00:19:55,121 --> 00:19:56,539
What did you say?

411
00:19:56,998 --> 00:20:00,084
Uh, wait. What do you mean by your home?

412
00:20:00,627 --> 00:20:02,420
[Louis] Exactly what I said.

413
00:20:02,503 --> 00:20:04,047
This was a wet market.

414
00:20:05,048 --> 00:20:07,133
I guess you could say I was raised here.

415
00:20:07,550 --> 00:20:09,761
Turned out the man that purchased me

416
00:20:09,844 --> 00:20:12,180
was the chairman
of the Horns Conglomerate.

417
00:20:12,263 --> 00:20:13,264
[sighs]

418
00:20:13,890 --> 00:20:15,516
You don't seem too surprised.

419
00:20:16,142 --> 00:20:18,478
Well, I was just trying
to match your energy.

420
00:20:18,561 --> 00:20:21,481
I felt like I should just
keep my snout shut and listen.

421
00:20:21,981 --> 00:20:24,067
[gentle music playing]

422
00:20:27,278 --> 00:20:29,906
[door creaking]

423
00:20:33,618 --> 00:20:37,580
[Ogma] <i>You, Louis,
you'll be able to change this world.</i>

424
00:20:39,916 --> 00:20:41,459
[Louis] I've made up my mind.

425
00:20:42,502 --> 00:20:44,504
I'm done playing the dutiful son.

426
00:20:44,921 --> 00:20:47,090
I'm ready to do whatever I have to.

427
00:20:48,174 --> 00:20:49,425
Louis,

428
00:20:50,301 --> 00:20:51,761
two days from now,

429
00:20:52,387 --> 00:20:54,597
I'm going to settle things with Melon.

430
00:20:54,681 --> 00:20:56,933
- So you did find Melon?
- Mmm.

431
00:20:57,475 --> 00:21:00,561
He's entering the turf war
as the boss of the Shishi-Gumi.

432
00:21:00,645 --> 00:21:02,772
So I signed up to fight him.

433
00:21:02,855 --> 00:21:04,941
Legoshi, do you know how dangerous it is?

434
00:21:05,024 --> 00:21:06,567
It's a real fight, you know.

435
00:21:06,651 --> 00:21:10,488
Ah. Well, that... I wanted to ask you...

436
00:21:11,489 --> 00:21:14,867
if anything happens to me, would you, uh...

437
00:21:14,951 --> 00:21:17,161
would you mind taking care of Haru?

438
00:21:17,245 --> 00:21:19,914
I know you fought Riz,
but this is very different.

439
00:21:20,581 --> 00:21:21,958
You can't do this alone.

440
00:21:22,542 --> 00:21:26,879
{\an8}[sighs] I want to face him
one-on-one, fair and square.

441
00:21:28,172 --> 00:21:29,590
{\an8}You want some help?

442
00:21:29,674 --> 00:21:30,967
{\an8}Huh?

443
00:21:31,926 --> 00:21:36,389
An herbivore with one leg
and the carnivore who devoured it.

444
00:21:37,390 --> 00:21:39,267
It seems like we'd make quite the pair.

445
00:21:40,143 --> 00:21:41,519
Uh, yeah.

446
00:21:43,938 --> 00:21:45,189
Right.

447
00:21:47,150 --> 00:21:48,943
That's exactly what this is.

448
00:21:50,361 --> 00:21:51,738
And you and me,

449
00:21:52,905 --> 00:21:54,407
we've got this.

450
00:22:00,997 --> 00:22:03,291
[closing theme song playing]
